S One of these problems includes the city-state 's lack of land space which would affect the structural design of the innovation particularly if it was on the large scale .
A 26 27|||R:DET|||a|||REQUIRED|||-NONE-|||0

S Another would be Singapore 's dense population that affects the location and structural considerations of the design process .

S Singapore currently has a land space 683 square kilometers , a country barely visible on the map .

S A strategy adopted by the government to solve this problem is land reclamation , which currently accounts for about 10 % of its land space .

S To further maximize land space , Singapore 's structures are mainly skyscrapers with strong and often costly foundations .

S This issue particularly affects innovations that are on the larger scale , as large cost will be incurred in the construction of its foundations .
