S An example would be the use of surveillance in this case radio frequency identification ( RFID ) technology in our everyday life without considering the health risks , consumer privacy rights and also its vulnerability to information thefts .

S With that the usage of RFID should be banned so as to safeguard the general public .

S Firstly the health issue poses a big threat to the usage of RFID as these chips are used in close vicinity to our body .

S Patients who wish to keep their medical information might chose to have the chip implanted right under their skin .
