S In the more developed regions , the number of persons aged over 60 would increase by 70 % from 231 million in 2000 to395 million in 2050 .

S These alarming statistics would bring about economic and societal problems to many developed countries .

S One of such is that the government might need to channel more revenue to meet the demands of the elderly group .
A 2 3|||R:OTHER|||problems|||REQUIRED|||-NONE-|||0

S In the long-term run , this can lead to shrinkage in the Gross Domestic Product ( GDP ) of the country or even affect the other sectors of development .
