S The populations of many countries are rapidly ageing as a result of declining fertility and increasing longevity .

S The group of 60 years or over is expected almost to triple , increasing from 673 million in 2005 and 2 billion by 2050 and the share of the elderly is also predicted to rise from 64 percent to nearly 80 percent in 2050 especially in developing countries ( Reilly 2007 ) .

