S And at the same time , World Bank economists estimated that for developed countries , public pension , which is only one term of the public spending on the aging problem , will increase from 9 percent of GDP in 1990 to 16 percent in 2040 ( Shaw , 2002 ) .

S Consequently , government may not be able to provide enough pension and health care to help improve the old citizens ' life as a result of lack of finance .
