S In this case , countries should invest more on the economy development or other areas to increase the financial ability so that old people can benefit more from the economic growth .

S Without restriction on the public spending on the elderly , the usage of the money may lose its effectiveness and may lead to further labor shortage , worsening the dilemma of aging process .

S Now OECD encourage United Kingdom to simplify the pension system and they argue that nowadays the pension system in UK may have negative effect on incentives for people to work and save ( OECD Supports Pension Reform in UK ) .
