S Hence it is inevitable that a significant amount of money has to be allocated to the funding of these facilities and the much needed pensions .

S So , public spending on the elderly should not be limited .

S Secondly , social problems may surface if the elderly do not receive sufficient care and help they need from the government .

S In Japan , pensioners constitute one-fifth of the country 's population .

