S Public Spending on Aged

S Singapore has one of the fastest aging populations in the world and is expected to be considered a country with an aging population by the year 2030 ( Chan , 2001 ) .

S This alarming trend is stimulated by declines in fertility rate , medical advances , and better health care which have resulted in longer life expectancy .
