S While a country has to focus on many sectors of development and most likely funding for the aged is not a prime concern , its funding should never be limited .

S In the coming years , as people live longer with each passing generation , our ageing population will climb steadily .

S Eventually becoming a group that 's too significant in numbers to ignore .

S If a country fails to take care of this significant portion of society , its people would lose confidence in government 's ability to handle other topics as well .

S Then , all other developments are futile as no amount of progress can replace a government 's credibility in its people 's heart .

