S Obviously , the older people use more healthcare than young people .

S Nevertheless , health costs are independent of the age structure , which defines the distribution of predetermined expenditures .

S Particularly , in Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development ( OECD ) , aging population does not have any connections to health expenditure as a part of GDP .

S For example , the over-65-year-old Swedish made up 17.3 % in 2000 , but Sweden just spent 8.6 % GDP on health .

S The former in Australia was 12.7 % , and the latter was 9.3 % , figured in 2001 and 2002 .

