S What is engineering psychology ?

S Generally speaking , engineering psychology is concerned with adapting equipment and environment to people ( Blum , 1952 ) .

S This adjustment is based on people 's psychological capacities and limitations , and the aim of it is to improve the overall system performance .

S The conception of engineering psychology is first brought out during the First World War , when people found that the efficiency of machines was reduced sharply when they were operated by women instead of men ( these machines are designed for men and not women ) .
