S As reported officially , " the Space Shuttle 's Solid Rocket Booster problem began with the faulty design of its joint and increased as both NASA and contractor management first failed to recognize it as a problem , then failed to fix it and finally treated it as an acceptable flight risk " .

S ( Dick , 1986 ) The cause of the accident therefore lies in technical deficiencies in design and human factors .

S Some expert ( Robert E. , 1997 ) claimed that the challenger accident was mainly caused by the mechanical failure due to the flaw of the original design .
