S Genetic testing is then carried out to determine if a person carries genes for certain inherited disorders .

S Of course , if the disorder is treatable , one would not worry so much about the consequences .

S However , if the disorder turns out to be non-treatable , the ethical issue as to whether the carrier of the known genetic risk is obligated to tell his or her relatives arises .

S Privacy and discrimination supports the fact that the carrier should not be obliged to disclose the information to his relatives .
