S As DNA technology advances , our ability to test individuals for genetic disorder is increasing significantly .
A 12 13|||R:NOUN:NUM|||disorders|||REQUIRED|||-NONE-|||0

S This new ability raises both high hopes and grave concerns .

S Genetic testing leads to diagnosis , prevention and treatment of a particular disease .

S Conversely , the implications of test results raise social and ethical concerns .

S The controversial issue on whether one should be obliged to disclose the result of such testing remains a subject of great concern among the society ( Mehlman , M,1999 ) Individual genetic information should not be revealed to third party without authorisation of the tested individual because the fundamental right to privacy should be respected .
